00:49:38.300 --> 00:49:40.173
Okay, gentlemen, right here.

00:49:43.960 --> 00:49:47.480
- [Nadeem] Hello, my name is Nadeem.

00:49:47.480 --> 00:49:52.423
Thank you very much for coming
and for the great lecture.

00:49:53.810 --> 00:49:58.810
My question is with respect
to energy and energy access

00:50:00.510 --> 00:50:04.943
with particular regard to
rural communities in Botswana.

00:50:06.460 --> 00:50:10.620
As you talk about a
knowledge-based economy,

00:50:10.620 --> 00:50:15.620
increased technology access, e-education,

00:50:15.870 --> 00:50:20.210
these things seem inherently
tied to energy access

00:50:20.210 --> 00:50:22.730
and reliable energy access.

00:50:22.730 --> 00:50:26.063
And I'm wondering what your
administration is doing,

00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:29.043
and perhaps, who you're partnering with,

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.473
to improve energy access in the country,

00:50:33.560 --> 00:50:36.160
to enable the knowledge based economy

00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:39.313
that you speak of to take root, thank you.

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:44.053
- It's a great question, great question.

00:50:45.596 --> 00:50:48.263
A, we're looking for more partners, right?

00:50:49.260 --> 00:50:50.380
But we're looking for partners

00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:53.270
that are creative and innovative.

00:50:53.270 --> 00:50:55.350
And you know why, because,

00:50:55.350 --> 00:50:58.783
some of the places that
do not have energy,

00:50:58.783 --> 00:51:00.266
or access to energy,

00:51:00.266 --> 00:51:04.253
are in far, remote, difficult to reach,

00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:07.603
lowly populated places.

00:51:08.870 --> 00:51:11.823
But with this enormity of sunlight,

00:51:12.860 --> 00:51:17.860
we think, the solution
would be solar, off grid.

00:51:18.950 --> 00:51:21.620
We have our integrated resource plan.

00:51:21.620 --> 00:51:23.450
And by the way, access to energy,

00:51:23.450 --> 00:51:26.000
and reliable energy is
quite high in Botswana now.

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:28.460
Rural electrification is pretty high,

00:51:28.460 --> 00:51:31.710
but the rate at which
settlements are growing,

00:51:31.710 --> 00:51:35.610
sometimes outstrips the supply capacity

00:51:35.610 --> 00:51:37.060
within a particular locality.

00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:41.330
But with the integrated resource plan,

00:51:41.330 --> 00:51:45.230
it would allow for those
who generate energy,

00:51:45.230 --> 00:51:50.230
excess energy from a solar
plant, to sell it to the grid.

00:51:50.690 --> 00:51:52.440
And the beautiful thing in
Southern Africa is that,

00:51:52.440 --> 00:51:56.350
we have an integrated exchange system

00:51:56.350 --> 00:51:59.040
for selling energy to other countries.

00:51:59.040 --> 00:52:00.350
So you can actually trade,

00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:04.100
and sell your energy to Zambia,
to Mozambique, and Lesotho,

00:52:04.100 --> 00:52:05.993
wherever there is a deficit.

00:52:07.320 --> 00:52:12.320
And we plan to be able to export energy

00:52:12.660 --> 00:52:14.870
within the next three years.

00:52:14.870 --> 00:52:16.490
Because we've floated tenders

00:52:17.504 --> 00:52:22.230
to generate 100 megawatts of energy

00:52:22.230 --> 00:52:25.610
from solar in additional, to what we have.

00:52:25.610 --> 00:52:30.610
And we will be licensing,

00:52:30.740 --> 00:52:33.923
independent power producers,
as they come and go.

00:52:34.770 --> 00:52:38.433
Rooftop solar systems are coming up.

00:52:39.890 --> 00:52:44.050
And so, any other new partners

00:52:44.050 --> 00:52:47.503
who come with new solutions, come see us.

00:52:49.850 --> 00:52:51.168
- [Eddie] Excellent.

00:52:51.168 --> 00:52:52.090
- We're a great country to
be in by the way.(laughs)

00:52:52.090 --> 00:52:52.923
I mean, just...

00:52:54.710 --> 00:52:57.873
We love visitors, we
take good care of you.

00:52:59.440 --> 00:53:00.470
We let you in and out.

00:53:00.470 --> 00:53:03.653
We let your money in and
out as you want, (laughs)

00:53:04.940 --> 00:53:08.533
in any currency, no exchange controls.

00:53:09.841 --> 00:53:11.220
And if you have excess money,

00:53:11.220 --> 00:53:13.460
you can just go down the street

00:53:13.460 --> 00:53:17.113
and buy some diamonds and
take them home.(laughs)

00:53:18.840 --> 00:53:19.970
- [Eddie] Excellent.

00:53:19.970 --> 00:53:24.120
Well, I am certain that there
will be many in this room

00:53:24.120 --> 00:53:28.120
and outside this will take
you up on your invitation,

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:32.200
to build stronger cooperation
and ties between us

00:53:32.200 --> 00:53:34.100
and the people of Botswana.

00:53:34.100 --> 00:53:35.520
Especially in your ambition

00:53:36.654 --> 00:53:37.487
to develop a knowledge-based economy.

00:53:37.487 --> 00:53:39.249
You've covered a lot of ground

00:53:39.249 --> 00:53:41.030
in your lecture and conversation today.

00:53:41.030 --> 00:53:44.773
Gender equity, climate
change, renewable energy,

00:53:45.880 --> 00:53:47.900
natural resource management,

00:53:47.900 --> 00:53:52.670
adding value in the supply
chain for people, education.

00:53:52.670 --> 00:53:57.670
But also importantly, your
vision for a non-aligned approach

00:53:58.811 --> 00:53:59.910
to your international engagement,

00:53:59.910 --> 00:54:02.670
to fulfill the priorities
and the needs of the people

00:54:02.670 --> 00:54:04.550
of Botswana through cooperation.

00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:06.930
And so, it is in that spirit,

00:54:06.930 --> 00:54:10.030
that we're delighted to
have you here on our campus,

00:54:10.030 --> 00:54:13.095
to set the stage and
articulate that vision.

00:54:13.095 --> 00:54:15.120
So, we're out of time

00:54:15.120 --> 00:54:19.090
for the lecture portion of this session,

00:54:19.090 --> 00:54:20.870
but, we would ask you

00:54:21.722 --> 00:54:23.840
